    "title": "Update: Suspicious package was smoke alarm, police say - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Emilie Raguso ,\n6 hours ago Update: Suspicious package was smoke alarm, police say Police closed the 1700 block of Shattuck Avenue in North Berkeley on Wednesday to investigate a \"suspicious suitcase\" making beeping noises, authorities report.\nPolice initially got the report about the suitcase behind some bushes on Shattuck Avenue near Virginia Street at about 12:10 p.m.\n\"Officers have closed off the street for vehicle and pedestrian traffic\" until Explosive Ordnance Disposal team members \"can evaluate the object,\" BPD said just after 1:30 p.m.\nPolice have closed a Berkeley block for a suspicious package, April 29, 2026. Ariel Nava Photo\nStay tuned for updates.\nUpdate, 3:33 p.m. Police reopened Shattuck Avenue at about 3:30 p.m. after determining that the beeping suitcase was due to a smoke alarm.",
    "summary": "6 hours ago Update: Suspicious package was smoke alarm, police say Police closed the 1700 block of Shattuck Avenue in North Berkeley on Wednesday to investigate a \"suspicious suitcase\" making beeping noises, authorities report. Police initially got the report about the suitcase behind some bushes on Shattuck Avenue near Virginia Street at about 12:10 p.m. \"Officers have closed off the street for vehicle and pedestrian traffic\" until Explosive Ordnance Disposal team members \"can evaluate the object,\" BPD said just after 1:30 p.m. Police have closed a Berkeley block for a suspicious package, April 29, 2026.",
